🚀 Feature
The JIT currently doesn't support for in for list elements.
i.e. this is not supported:
@torch.jit.script
def fn(a, b):
    # type: (List[int]) -> int
	sum = torch.zeros_like(b[0])
	for item in b:
		sum += item
	return sum
Currently, the un-ergonomic workaround is:
@torch.jit.script
def fn(a, b):
    # type: (List[int]) -> int
	sum = torch.zeros_like(b[0])
	for i in range(len(b)):
		sum += b[i]
	return sum

