🐛 Bug
The released Windows binaries for LibTorch CUDA 10 include CUDA and CuDNN DLLs, suggesting they were built with CUDA/CuDNN support, but torch::cuda::cudnn_is_available() returns false.
In the past it was possible to work around this by copying files from a Windows/Anaconda python installation of pytorch, but this no longer works.
